_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojw28/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/238569330","html_url":"https://github.com/google/ExoPlayer/issues/1712#issuecomment-238569330","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/1712","id":238569330,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIzODU2OTMzMA==","user":{"login":"cstew","id":42011,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyMDEx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42011?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cstew","html_url":"https://github.com/cstew","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cstew/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cstew/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cstew/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cstew/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cstew/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cstew/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cstew/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cstew/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cstew/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-08-09T14:24:29Z","updated_at":"2016-08-09T14:24:29Z","body":"The video creation and hosting is fully outside of my control. It is good to know that an external `.srt` file will render correctly. I may have to go that route. \n\nIt is important to note that the vendor that is supplying the video to me is not using Handbrake to embed the subtitles into the video (they are using some other video encoding software). \n\nI've been doing some more digging this morning and it seems that the font tag issue may not be the actual cause of the problem. I see erroneous characters in the subtitles if there are more than 32 characters per subtitle. \n\n```\n1\n00:00:01,468 --> 00:00:03,068\nSubtitle test\n\n2\n00:00:03,070 --> 00:00:04,710\nThis is a slightly longer captio\n\n3\n00:00:04,705 --> 00:00:05,505\nThis is a slightly longer caption\n\n4\n00:00:05,506 --> 00:00:08,506\nThis is a slightly longer \ncaption2\n```\n\nLines 1 and 2 display correctly. Lines 3 and 4 show an additional character when the subtitles are displayed. \n\nBelow is the video that reproduces the problem and the `.srt` file that I encoded into it. \n\nVideo: https://www.dropbox.com/s/v3wwk56qmu7h5xz/video.mp4?dl=1\nSubtitle file: https://www.dropbox.com/s/5is3b7rb3zee2i3/subs.srt?dl=1\n\n![device-2016-08-09-072316](https://cloud.githubusercontent.com/assets/42011/17519774/2d50b4c6-5e02-11e6-9467-b24115320a82.png)\n\nIs this by design? Maybe there is a limit to how many characters can exist per subtitle row in the spec?\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/google/ExoPlayer/issues/comments/238569330/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"cstew","id":42011,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyMDEx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42011?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cstew","html_url":"https://github.com/cstew","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cstew/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cstew/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cstew/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cstew/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.g